{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fapi2"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"ClientProfile.fapi2","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fapi2"}],"roleHeading":"Case","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"case","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13ClientProfileO5fapi2yA2CmF"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/fapi2"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/fapi2","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"title":"AxiamSDK"},"Self::Standard":{"type":"link","title":"Standard","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Standard"}],"url":"Self::Standard","identifier":"Self::Standard"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ClientProfile","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Which security posture a client is registered under (X5.1). This is the FAPI “one switch”."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"FAPI 2.0 is not a single feature but a bundle of constraints — mandatory PAR, mandatory PKCE"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"S256"},{"text":", mandatory strong client authentication, mandatory sender-constrained tokens,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a refusal of every relaxation the base specs permit. Encoding them as one profile rather","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than a dozen independent booleans means an operator cannot register a client that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"nearly"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" FAPI, and a reviewer can answer “is this client financial-grade?” by reading one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field. The same philosophy as the rate-limit postures: ordinary clients see no behaviour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change at all, because ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"Self::Standard"},{"text":" is the serde default and every row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before schema v38 decodes to it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile/fapi2":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fapi2","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/fapi2","title":"ClientProfile.fapi2","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/fapi2","kind":"symbol"}}}